So every ELF has the same verdict and the same cycle count on both RTLs, consistent with none of the
2,578 tests reaching a path the branch changed (8-byte access split by an NA4/TOR boundary, PTE access
split the same way, viota.m with an LMUL-misaligned vs2, a .vf scalar that is not NaN-boxed at SEW=32).
ACT therefore neither confirms nor contradicts those fixes; riscv-dv vs Spike and the directed core
tests (pmp_partial_directed, vec_directed 25, fpvec_directed 11) cover them.

